# {{PACK_NAME}}

A sample Kindgi pack in Java — scaffolded by `kindgi init --template=java`.

Two tools (`echo`, `greet`), one guardrail (`response-not-empty`), one agent
that uses both tools and the guardrail, and one flow that runs the echo tool.

## Layout

```
{{PACK_NAME}}/
├── kindgi.config.json                       # the pack's id and version ("language": "java")
├── pom.xml                                  # com.kindgi:kindgi-pack, Java 17
├── src/main/java/{{JAVA_PACKAGE_PATH}}/
│   ├── tools/Echo.java                      # Tool.define — records in, records out
│   ├── tools/Greet.java                     # Tool.define
│   ├── guardrails/ResponseNotEmpty.java     # Guardrail.define — a zero-LLM check over the run
│   ├── agents/EchoAgent.java                # Agent.define — data
│   └── flows/EchoFlow.java                  # Flow.define — data
└── src/test/java/{{JAVA_PACKAGE_PATH}}/ToolsTest.java   # the tools, called directly
```

## Run

You need a JDK 17 or later (`JAVA_HOME`); Maven comes with the project
(`./mvnw`).

```sh
./mvnw test
kindgi dev       # boots Kindgi locally, compiles and runs this pack, recompiling on save
```

Then, from another terminal:

```sh
kindgi runs start --agent={{PACK_ID}}.echo-agent --input='{"userMessage":"hi"}'
```

`kindgi dev` uses `JAVA_HOME`'s JDK (or `dev.javaHome` in `kindgi.config.json`)
and the project's Maven wrapper (or `dev.maven`, e.g. `["mvn", "-s", "settings.xml"]`).
`MAVEN_ARGS` and `MAVEN_OPTS` in your shell reach Maven only, never the pack.

## Use a real model

`kindgi dev` gives a new pack `dev-echo`, a fallback provider that isn't a
model: it calls the first tool and replies "Tool responded: …", after a
warning line that says so. It answers only while no other provider fits. To
use a real model, set one LLM provider's key and register its preset, with
`kindgi dev` running, from another terminal. For Claude:

```sh
kindgi secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY --env=local --scope=tenant   # no-echo prompt; writes .env.local
kindgi providers register --preset=anthropic                      # Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 4.5
```

Claude takes over from dev-echo on the next turn; nothing to restart.
OpenAI (`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `--preset=openai`), Gemini (`GEMINI_API_KEY`,
`--preset=gemini-api`), Groq (`GROQ_API_KEY`, `--preset=groq`) and
OpenRouter (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `--preset=openrouter`) work the same way;
`kindgi providers presets` lists the presets.

## Build

`kindgi build --env=<name>` makes the pack's image: Maven compiles it in a
pinned Maven + JDK 17 image, the index is built in the image, and the pack
service runs on a JRE 17 as its entrypoint.
